From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:31:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): observe fleet review verdicts and fence stored
 cap provenance [daveey]

Review #3742 at 6993cc found two behavior defects and stale network-budget docs.
Why merge remained unreachable: independent sessions share one GitHub login and
publish COMMENTED verdicts; treating GitHub identity as independent-session proof
excluded the real approval source. Flow now observes first-line explicit verdicts
on commit-bound reviews, with latest-verdict, bot, boundary and head controls.
This is display evidence only; ship's independent-session authorization is unchanged.
A live read of PR #3722 confirms the shared-login bold Verdict shape at its head.

Why stored cap evaluation failed open: a missing creator in row_opts inherited
the evaluating worker's creator environment through the creation-only fallback.
Mark stored provenance and never exempt a creator-less stored card via env.
Creation-context exemptions and persisted explicit creators retain behavior.

Proof: 8 new regressions RED on previous head. Eight consumer files: 1683 passed,
0 failed. Final targets/docs: 57 passed, 0 failed. Mutation baseline 54 passed;
9/9 mutants killed, covering stored marker/guard, explicit creator, fleet verdict,
bots, current head, change-request supersession and first-line/token boundaries.
Full scripts/check: 21 checks ok. No production limits enabled or Desktop restart.
